course: world
lesson: 36
title: Healthy food, water and vitamins
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Food gives the body energy and the materials it needs to grow and to repair itself. No single food has everything, so we need a mix of foods: a balanced diet.
explain: Carbohydrates (bread, rice, potatoes, pasta) give energy; proteins (meat, fish, eggs, beans, milk) build and repair the body; fats (oil, butter, nuts) store energy and keep us warm, but we need only a little.
explain: Fruit and vegetables give vitamins, minerals and fibre. For example, vitamin C from oranges and peppers helps the body heal, and calcium from milk builds bones.
explain: More than half of your body is water. We lose water every day in sweat, breath and urine, so we must drink it every day; water carries food in the blood, cools us by sweating and washes out waste.
explain: Sugary drinks and sweets give quick energy but almost nothing else, so they are foods for sometimes, not for every day.
fact: A balanced diet is a mix of foods from all the food groups.
fact: Carbohydrates, such as bread, rice and potatoes, give the body energy.
fact: Proteins, such as meat, fish, eggs and beans, build and repair the body.
fact: Fats give energy and keep us warm, but we need only a small amount.
fact: Fruit and vegetables give vitamins, minerals and fibre.
fact: Vitamin C, found in oranges, lemons, peppers and berries, helps the body heal and fight illness.
fact: Calcium, found in milk and cheese, builds strong bones and teeth.
fact: More than half of the human body is water.
fact: We lose water every day in sweat, breath and urine.
fact: A person can live for weeks without food but only for a few days without water.
fact: Too much sugar can cause tooth decay and too much weight.
fact: Long ago sailors without fresh fruit got sick with scurvy because they lacked vitamin C.
exercise: What is a balanced diet? | Foods from all the food groups | Eating only fruit, because fruit is healthy | Eating the same food every day of the week | Eating as much as possible at every meal
exercise: Which foods are rich in carbohydrates? | Bread, rice and potatoes | Fish, eggs and beans for dinner | Butter and oil | Water and tea
exercise: What is the main job of protein? | To build and repair the body | To give the food its colour | To cool the body down when it gets hot | To help us see in the dark
exercise: Which foods are rich in protein? | Meat, fish, eggs and beans | Sugar, sweets and fizzy drinks | Apples, lettuce and cucumber | Water, juice and fruit squash
exercise: What do fruit and vegetables give us? | Vitamins, minerals and fibre | Mostly fat and sugar for quick energy | Mostly protein | Nothing useful
exercise: Which vitamin is found in oranges and peppers? | Vitamin C | Vitamin K only | No vitamin at all | Calcium
exercise: What does calcium help to build? | Bones and teeth | Hair and nails only | Fat under the skin | The lungs
exercise: About how much of the human body is water? | More than half | About a tenth | Almost none | All of it
exercise: How does the body lose water every day? | In sweat, breath and urine | Only when we cry or get very upset | Only in hot countries | It never loses water
exercise: How long can a person live without water? | Only a few days | Several months if it rests | A whole year or even longer | For ever, water is not needed
exercise: Why should sweets be eaten only sometimes? | They give energy but almost nothing else and harm teeth | They have too much protein | They are full of vitamins | They make bones too heavy
exercise: Which food group should we eat only a little of? | Fats | Vegetables | Fruit | Water
exercise: What illness did old sailors get from lacking vitamin C? | Scurvy | Chickenpox | A cold | Measles
exercise: How does water help to cool us? | It leaves the skin as sweat and takes heat away | It freezes inside the body and cools us from within | It blocks the Sun's rays | It turns into fat
test: A runner wants energy for a long race. Which meal helps most the evening before? | A plate of pasta with vegetables | A bowl of sweets | A glass of oil | Only a glass of water
test: Tim eats chips and burgers every day and never fruit or vegetables. What is his diet missing? | Vitamins, minerals and fibre | Fat from the oil the chips are fried in | Energy to run around and play all day | Salt, which chips and burgers lack
test: A child broke a leg. Which foods help most to repair the bone? | Milk, cheese and protein foods | Crisps and fizzy drinks | Sweets and cakes | Only water and ice
test: Why do we feel thirsty after playing football in the heat? | We lost water by sweating | Our muscles turned into water | Our stomach made too much water | The ball took our water
test: Which is true? | No single food gives the body everything it needs | Fruit alone gives everything the body needs to grow and stay well | Fat is the only food we need | Water has lots of energy in it
test: Long ago, a ship carried lemons for the sailors. Why? | Lemons gave vitamin C and kept away scurvy | Lemons were used to clean the deck | Lemons gave the sailors protein | Lemons kept the water from freezing
test: Which lunchbox is most balanced? | A cheese sandwich, an apple, carrot sticks and water | Three chocolate bars, a packet of biscuits and a big cola | A bag of crisps and a cake | Only a big bottle of juice
test: Why is water important even though it gives no energy? | It carries food in the blood and washes out waste | It gives us protein | It builds our bones | It replaces our food completely
test: why do sailors long ago get sick on ships with no fruit | They lacked vitamin C and got scurvy | The sea salt made them sick | They ate too much fruit before leaving | They got too much sun on deck
test: footy match tomorrow, what do i eat for energy | Carbohydrates like pasta, rice or bread | Only salad leaves and water | A big bag of sweets | Nothing, hungry players run faster
test: Max says you can go weeks without water but not without food. true? | No, without water we last only days | Yes, food matters much more than water does | Yes, the body makes all its own water inside | No, you can go weeks without both of them
test: my nan says fat is always bad and we need none. right? | No, we need a small amount for energy and warmth | Yes, any fat at all is harmful | Yes, fat only makes us heavy | No, we need fat more than anything else
exam: Identify the principal function of proteins in the diet. | The building and repair of the body | The provision of fibre | The prevention of scurvy among sailors at sea | The retention of water
exam: Identify the vitamin whose deficiency caused scurvy among sailors. | Vitamin C | Vitamin D | Vitamin A | Vitamin B
exam: Select the response that is consistent with the established facts concerning survival without nourishment. | A person may survive weeks without food but only days without water | A person may survive weeks without water but only days without food | A person may survive equally long without either | A person may survive indefinitely without water
exam: State the proportion of the human body composed of water. | More than one half | Less than one tenth | Approximately one quarter | The entirety
